     \coprod_{(u:i\to j)} D(i)\rightrightarrows\coprod_i D(i)\longrightarrow\operatorname{colim}D.
     \]
     Since \(G\) preserves the two required coproducts and coequalizers, it preserves this presentation and hence every \(J\)-shaped colimit. This is the coproduct–coequalizer construction used in [LimitsOfProductsAndEqualizers](https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/blob/master/Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Limits/Constructions/LimitsOfProductsAndEqualizers.lean).

